// This node's own checkpoint: a match whose arms are all class patterns
// raises a real, reachable MATCH_ERROR when no arm matches. The compiler
// never proves a class pattern exhaustive over its own subclasses (unlike
// an enum's constructor set, checkEnumExhaustiveness does not run for a
// class pattern at all), so a value of an unrelated class reaching this
// match is ordinary, in-language behavior, not a corner case.
class A {}
class B {}

print "before";
print match A() {
    case B => "b"
};
